1. The minimum bid increment is 10 S.T Points. 
2. Place(s): number of the predetermined winner places in the auction. Every winner can get 1 item by offering the highest price(s). For example, if the number of buyers is 3, then the 3 highest bidders will get 1 item respectively;
3. Depending on the number of places, at the start of each auction, a liminted number of bidders can bid at the starting price. For example, if there are 2 places, the first 2 bidders can bid at the starting price, and if there are 3 places, the first 3, and so on;
4. If all the buyers' places are taken, only the bids higher than the lowest standing price will be accepted to challenge;
5. Every user can only have one bid, which is the highest of all his/her bids;
6. If your bid is lower than the lowest standing price, the S.T Points you bid will be returned to your account automatically;
7. If you want to bid again as an expected winner in the auction, the price should be higher than your current one with enough S.T Points balance. Once you bid successfully, your current bid will be returned to your account automatically.

